course: dictionary
lesson: 15536
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word suite can mean a set of rooms, a set of furniture, a piece of music or a set of computer programs. Context tells you which meaning is right. «The hotel gave us a suite with its own bedroom and sitting room.» Bedroom and sitting room are clues that suite means a set of rooms.
explain: «We chose a new three-piece suite for the lounge.» The lounge and the word furniture clues tell you suite means matching furniture, not rooms. Three-piece means it has three parts: a sofa and two armchairs.
explain: «The orchestra played The Planets Suite.» Here a suite is a piece of music made of several shorter parts played one after another. Music words such as orchestra are your clue. Always check: does my meaning fit the sentence?
fact: Suite is a noun, and one spelling can have several meanings.
fact: «Suite» can mean a set of rooms that go together, as in «hotel suite».
fact: «Suite» can mean matching furniture, as in «three-piece suite».
fact: «Suite» can mean a piece of music with several shorter parts, as in «The Nutcracker Suite».
fact: «Suite» can mean a set of computer programs that work together, as in «office suite».
exercise: «The hotel gave us a suite overlooking the beach.» What does suite mean here? | *A set of rooms that go together | A type of sofa | A computer program | A piece of music
exercise: «The music teacher played a suite of short dances.» What does suite mean here? | A kind of hotel | *A piece of music made of several short parts | A set of matching furniture | A room with computers
exercise: «Our school has a new computer suite.» Which meaning fits best? | A set of rooms in a hotel | *A room full of computers | A piece of music | A sofa and two armchairs
test: Mum said the new three-piece suite fits in the lounge. What is a three-piece suite? | *A sofa and two armchairs | Three pieces of music | A set of three rooms | A computer with three programs
test: «The office suite on the computer has a word processor and a spreadsheet.» What does suite mean here? | *A set of programs that work together | A piece of music | A room for meetings | A bedroom with a sitting room
exam: Which sentence uses suite to mean a piece of music? | *«The orchestra played The Planets Suite.» | «The hotel suite had two bedrooms.» | «Dad bought a new office suite.» | «The bathroom suite is white.»
